one of the president's main agenda items  as you just heard there  is north korea denuclearization a big  part of that effort is south korean  president  moon jae-in who just wrapped up his own  meeting with chairman kim in north korea  i talked with the south korean president  earlier today  yesterday president trump before the  signing of the new trade agreement  said this a lot of very positive things  are happening with chairman kim  of north korea do you expect another  summit between president trump and  chairman kim  in coming weeks well i would say  yes i traveled to pyongyang last week  and had a very good  meeting with chairman kim and through  the  summit meeting we had achieved some  progress on denuclearization  and i look forward uh to a summit a  meeting taking place between chairman  kim  and president trump in the not too  distant future before the end of the  year  yes i believe so mr president there is  concern  in the u.s that maybe too much is being  given  up before actual denuclearization is  happening  in north korea how do you address that  there are many skeptical voices as to  whether north korea will actually keep  their promise  this time and however i have to tell you  that  the agreement that we have right now is  actually completely different  from what we had in the past for the  first time in history  you have seen the president of the  united states and the supreme leader of  north korea  threshold an agreement through a summit  meeting and they  made a promise in front of the whole  world to  which is binding and they have lots of  responsibility on their shoulders i  believe that this  promise will be kept in terms of north  korea  they can only have sanctions relief  after denuclearization is completed  and through this they can have the  economic recovery that they are desiring  as for president trump he needs to solve  the north korean nuclear problem  and this is a problem that nobody had  been able to solve in the decades past  so  through this he will be able to have a  major achievement  which is your top priority reunification  or denuclearization my priority is  peace and if we have solid peace then i  believe that  unification will come naturally as well  and  in order to achieve peace the  prerequisite would be  denuclearization what is your  relationship with president trump  and how would you describe him  ever since my inauguration last may i  had  seven summit meetings with president  trump as well as  more than 20 phone calls i can tell you  that  i've become more than a friend with  president trump and between the two of  us  there is absolutely perfect trust and  when you uh  think about what president trump has  accomplished  in terms of north korea's  denuclearization you just have to look  at  the changes that have been in place  during the nine months ever since  last november and if you compare what  president trump said during his speech  at the un general assembly last year  rocket man is on a suicide mission for  himself and for his regime and  what he'll be saying today tremendous  progress has been made  and i think you're going to see an  outcome then you'll be able to  distinguish the differences and ever  since last november  uh north korea has not been has not  engaged in any nuclear or  missile test and or any provocations of  this kind  and they have already uh permanently  dismantled the nuclear test site in  congedi and this is actually  the only nuclear test site they have  which means that they will not be able  to  have another nuclear test in the future  and during my summit meeting with  chairman kim  in pyongyang last week he also expressed  his willingness to permanently dismantle  uh the missile engine test site and the  launch platform in tong tangi  under observation of american experts  and  when he implements these measures this  will mean that  north korea will not be able to test  long-range missiles again  so now all of this means that north  korea  will not be able to threaten the united  states with  their nuclear or missile arsenal he  is actually willing to take additional  measures  including the dismantlement of the  nuclear  cases and all of this change that we are  witnessing right now  was possible because the  president of the united states decided  to have uh the first  ever summit with the leader of  north korea in 70 years of their history  all of my praise goes to president trump  so you give him a lot of credit  yes you've met with chairman kim more  than  most people in the world  how do you describe him his  sensibilities  is he serious do you really believe that  he could denuclearize his the north  fully or is that something that really  is the identity  of north korea chairman kim  has a great uh has unwavering trust and  expectations for president trump and  uh he is also aware that um the complete  denuclearization  of north korea at such a major feat can  only be achieved by someone like  president trump  so chairman kim actually wants within  to achieve the complete denuclearization  of north korea  with president trump within his first  term in office  and he has expressed this commitment  this desire on many occasions too so in  order to  make progress he wants to have the  second  u.s north korea summit as soon as  possible i would say that  chairman kim is young but he's candid  and he also has clear commitment  to to denuclearization and he is now  ready to abandon his nuclear program  and focus on economic development  instead in order to  help his people he has this kind of a  strategic mind  so um he is looking forward  to achieving complete denuclearization  with president trump  and afterwards receive economic  assistance  do you think that full verifiable  denuclearization the goal of january  2021  that has been talked about is that  realistic  seems like a lot to go in a short period  of time  during my summit meeting in pyongyang  chairman kim  mentioned he is willing to have the  international inspectors  inspect these activities he said that  he's willing to  permanently dismantle the related  facilities in a verifiable way  so i believe that i have ascertained uh  chairman kim's  commitment to a complete  denuclearization uh therefore  um now if north korea  takes a genuine measures in terms of uh  dismantling their nuclear pro  program it all comes down to whether the  united states  is ready to provide corresponding  measures in a swift way  for the united states they promise to  end  its hostile relations with with north  korea to provide  security guarantees and also work  towards new  u.s north korea relations so although  all these actions would not happen  simultaneously  broadly i believe that these actions  need to be taken in parallel  if the united states could provide this  kind of trust i believe that we will be  able to accelerate  the denuclearization process this this  is why i believe that  the denuclearization is achievable  within the first term of president  trump's term do you trust chairman kim  from a u.s perspective he does not have  a great track record of promising and  then  delivering on things  so what we hear from the u.s  administration  is that they would like to see things  done completely  and then pull the sanctions off when we  say corresponding measures  this doesn't only allude to a sanctions  relief  we could think about the declaration to  end the korean war  or humanitarian assist assistance or the  exchanges  uh well the cultural and artistic  exchanges  and such kind of non-political exchanges  so we could think about establishing a a  u.s  liaison office in pyongyang and by  establish  establishing this kind of office we can  show  the u.s commitment to end hostile  relations with north korea  and also logistically support uh the the  activities of the the inspectors and we  could also think about  exchanging economic delegations with  north korea  i can tell you that there is nothing to  lose for us  when we put our trust in north korea and  the measures that north korea will be  taking  will be will be the permanent  dismantlement of  nuclear test site the missile engine  test site  nuclear bases and its existing nuclear  arsenal these  are all irreversible measures however  the measures  the united states and the republic of  korea will be taking would be measures  such as  the suspension of joint military  exercises which can be resumed at any  time  and also the end of war declaration can  be  revoked any time as well if north korea  goes back on its promise then we can put  on these sanctions once again  the united states has nothing to lose do  you envision  seeing one korea in your lifetime  well it is very difficult to predict  when  unification will be achieved we cannot  really plan for this kind of thing  i believe that if we establish complete  peace then we will be able to see one  day  all of a sudden the unification come and  i'm hopeful  that i'll be able to see it within my  lifetime the u.s has had troops on the  korean peninsula for 60 plus years  do you want to see u.s troops leave  sooner rather than later could it  challenge him i would say no  i can tell you that the u.s forces in  korea not only  is beneficial for our deterrence  vis-a-vis north korea  but also it's playing a lynchpin role in  terms of upholding peace and  stability in the northeast asian  region as a whole even after the peace  treaty side and even after unification  is achieved i can see the u.s forces in  korea  remain in place for the as peace and  stability of the north east asian region  you mentioned the end of war  declaration do you expect to sign that  at this next summit with president trump  i had ample discussions with president  trump on this issue  during my summit yesterday and i expect  there will be  plenty of discussions between president  trump and chairman kim  in the upcoming u.s north korea summit  it is  my desire to assign this as soon as  possible  to give a symbol that the  hostile relations between the united  states and north korea have been ended  and i believe that there is a basic  sympathy regarding this view  i want you to address some of your  critics uh  in korea um a couple of  points they say that you've been  clamping down  on journalists and and muzzling north  korean defectors  and your critics say that that you're  undermining free speech there  and and democratic norms how do you  respond to that  yeah well i can tell you that maybe um  out of the entire history of the  republic fair uh the  freedom of speech and the freedom of  press have never been uh greater  than this time and and even uh the kind  of fake news  that you're seeing in among the press  and among the sns  and they go unpunished as well and every  weekend you can see uh in  the uh kuala lumen plaza which is just  right in front of my  uh office you can see um the assemblies  that  heavily criticize me happen every  weekend your critics are their theory is  that you're trying to line south korea  up  with north korea in getting ready for  reunification  to the extent of even taking freedom out  of textbooks  uh not tying it to democracy so you say  in the words of president trump that's  all fake  our news of improving relations with  north korea and  aspiring for unification is actually the  same across  all administrations and the our  constitution  actually prescribes that we need to work  towards  achieving peaceful reunification with  north korea and it is one of the prime  responsibilities  of a president and as for the people who  criticize me  i can tell you that most of them are  people who  in past and administrations had been  calling reunification  as some kind of a bonanza but now they  are turning on me because  the the the government has changed mr  president we appreciate your time  yes thank you

